zbd (2.0.0~dev1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the refactored zbd 2.0 development
    branch. The codebase has been split into:
      - a hardened oneshot system service (zbd-system) that applies
        battery threshold, backlight and DMIC defaults at boot,
      - a user-session GTK tray (zbd-tray) that owns the runtime
        monitors (Bluetooth, USB, iio-sensor-proxy).
  * Pluggable display backends (xrandr / gdctl) so the daemon works
    on both X11 and Wayland-with-GNOME (default on Ubuntu 26.04).
  * Strict configuration validation, shell-free command execution,
    proper SIGINT/SIGTERM handling, criterion-based unit tests,
    -fPIE -pie -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now release builds.
  * Replaces the historical single-binary layout that mixed the
    privileged operations and the user-facing GTK code in one
    process.

 -- marcos <marcos@anexa.net>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 20:30:00 +0200
